I've ascended about a dozen times and I know the formula pretty well.
I do things in a certain order because I know that if I try them out of
order them I'm taking a risk.  I usually drive down to Gnome Town in
the mines prior to doing Sokoban.  I never go below Gnome Town until I
have an AC below 0 and either MR or Reflection.

This time I randomly drew a Valkyrie.  Nothing had proven any danger so
far except for hunger.  I had Excaliber from dipping and I was around
XL 8.  I hit Gnome Town and found a BoH and an MM, but no wishes.  I
was having such an easy time of it that I actually changed my mind on
the way to the upstairs and went to the downstairs instead.  I was
going to drive down quick and snatch the luckstone before continuing.
I also had found a leash earlier and was hoping to find a poly trap.

Literally, within two moves of going to the level blow I was hit once
with a lightning wand.  I did not have teleport identified, the mines
were dark and I had only a direction from whence the lightning came,
and the first shot didn't hurt me enough to make praying viable.
However, I knew that another shot was going to kill me.  I took one
more step up, hoping to take me out of a shooting angle only to get
hammered by the second shot.

YAStupidD.  I knew better and went down anyway.  The RNG takes delight
in punishing me for my arrogance.  Let this be a lesson to young
Nethackers, The RNG giveth and the RNG cackles while it smoketh your
ass.



